<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lewanika</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1842–<a href="/years/1916">1916</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Lubosi Lewanika</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lewanika was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/litunga">Litunga</a>, or king, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Lozi</a> of Barotseland in present-day western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a> from 1878, with a brief interruption, until 1916. Seeking protection against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> and the Portuguese, he signed concessions with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a> from 1890. These became the basis of company rule in North-Western Rhodesia and of Barotseland's special status within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lewanika.jpg" alt="Lewanika" width="320" height="527" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: G.H. Tod · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lewanika_in_Edinburgh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
